prompt:
Use case: style-transfer / precise-object-edit. The input is the existing OpenVegas basketball completion animation to revise. Keep its crisp high-quality outlined pixel-sprite look, coral shooter kit and teal defender kit, but REPLACE BOTH characters with athletic ADULT MEN with short hair. No women, no ponytails, no robots, no celebrities, no branding.
Rebuild the composition as a fixed BIRD'S-EYE TOP-DOWN basketball half-court view, looking steeply down so the floor's court geometry is unmistakable. All 12 cells use that SAME overhead camera. Draw a charcoal-dark court with clear cream-white THREE-POINT ARC curving around the basket at the RIGHT; paint and key nearer the basket, boundary lines. Shooter far LEFT clearly OUTSIDE/BEHIND the three-point arc by at least a full shoe-length, never on the line; basket far RIGHT. Defender at the CENTER inside the arc, at least 3 character body widths from shooter, never adjacent. Distinct readable male human sprites drawn with tasteful elevated arcade perspective on the top-down court, not mere circles or flat tokens. Wide separation and visible arc are essential.
Production 4-column by 3-row equal-cell sprite sheet, EXACTLY TWELVE distinct chronological frames, ordered rows left-to-right:
1 overhead establishing view: full 3-point arc, shooter holding ball outside arc left, defender center far away, hoop right;
2 shooter dribbles at that same outside-arc position;
3 gathers ball with both feet still behind line;
4 knees bend into shooting stance, no stepping over arc;
5 jumps vertically to release long-range three-point shot from outside arc;
6 follow-through with ball above court traveling toward hoop;
7 basketball nearly at right-hand rim, both men watching;
8 unmistakable swish/net movement at far-right hoop;
9 shooter lands at original outside-arc spot, defender drops hands;
10 shooter turns slightly in celebratory side-step;
11 shooter raises three fingers with other arm bent in a dance;
12 composed triumphant original pose with three fingers aloft.
Each cell must include the SAME full overhead court, arc, hoop and clearly separated male players. Lock floor markings, camera, colors, character identities, court placement and scale throughout. Both feet behind the 3-point line visible before release. Court court court, not the old sideview wooden plank. No close-ups or camera cuts. Flat dark charcoal background for court; true alpha outside the rectangular court tile if any; NO fake checkerboard, NO grid borders, NO labels, text or watermarks. Pixel edges sharp, generous margins to avoid clipping.

